  "description": "This bullaun stone was described by Carrigan (1905) as a \"holy water font\" which had been carried \"about a century ago\" from the churchyard to the north of the churchyard. It is now on private land, but I had permission to scan it. Since Walter O'Keeffe carried it and challenged anyone to bring it back to the churchyard, it qualifies as a lifting stone. Carrigan writes that it weighs about 6cwt which makes it one of the heaviest in the country. Walter O'Keeffe died in October 18th 1752 aged 21 which dates his lift to before that date.\n\nSMR no.: KK020-017007-\n\nMade in KiriEngine from 77 images.",
